  "slug": "class-imbalance-calibration-clinical-tabular",
  "direction": "Handling class imbalance without breaking calibration, on small public clinical tabular datasets bundled with scikit-learn (breast cancer Wisconsin; and artificially imbalanced versions at 1:5, 1:20 and 1:50). Compare no correction, class reweighting, random oversampling, SMOTE (implemented directly) and decision-threshold moving, for logistic regression and gradient boosting. Report AUROC, AUPRC, Brier score and calibration slope: which corrections help discrimination and which only distort predicted risk?",
